github.com/seonho12-54/qodo-coderabbit-benchmark/pull/6235#issuecomment-5534690094","viewerDidAuthor":true},{"id":"IC_kwDOUMmgW88AAAABSeTMLQ","author":{"login":"qodo-code-review"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"<h3>Code Review by Qodo</h3>\n\n<code>🐞 Bugs (1)</code>  <code>📘 Rule violations (0)</code>  <code>📜 Skill insights (0)</code>\n\n<img src=\"https://www.qodo.ai/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/light-grey-line.svg\" height=\"10%\" alt=\"Grey Divider\">\n\n<br/>\n\n<img src=\"https://img.shields.io/badge/High-634FD1?style=flat-square\" height=\"20px\" alt=\"Action required\">\n\n<details>\n<summary>  1.  Explicit OPTIONS enablement broken <code>🐞 Bug</code> <code>≡ Correctness</code></summary>\n\n<br/>\n\n> <details open>\n><summary>Description</summary>\n><br/>\n>\n><pre>\n>When <b><i>provide_automatic_options=True</i></b> is supplied directly or through a view attribute, the new\n><b><i>None</i></b> guard skips adding <b><i>OPTIONS</i></b> to the rule&#x27;s methods. Routing therefore rejects OPTIONS with\n>405 before Flask can generate the promised automatic response.\n></pre>\n></details>\n\n> <details>\n><summary>Code</summary>\n><br/>\n>\n><code>[src/flask/sansio/app.py[R638-641]](https://github.com/seonho12-54/qodo-coderabbit-benchmark/pull/6235/files#diff-c57b8f34cffef9948b35aec94cb2364f75c1a2854064a13bf8216603cb1f607bR638-R641)</code>\n>\n>```diff\n>+        if provide_automatic_options is None:\n>+            if \"OPTIONS\" not in methods and self.config[\"PROVIDE_AUTOMATIC_OPTIONS\"]:\n>+                provide_automatic_options = True\n>+                required_methods.add(\"OPTIONS\")\n>```\n></details>\n\n> <details>\n><summary>Evidence</summary>\n><br/>\n>\n><pre>\n>The public contract says this parameter adds OPTIONS and handles it automatically, but the changed\n>branch adds OPTIONS only while resolving a <b><i>None</i></b> value. The resulting rule can have its automatic\n>flag set to true without accepting OPTIONS, and dispatch raises any routing exception before\n>checking that flag; class-based views also propagate explicit values through the same path.\n></pre>\n>\n> <code>[src/flask/sansio/scaffold.py[408-437]](https://github.com/seonho12-54/qodo-coderabbit-benchmark/blob/56a0ec00080153af0afed3b70b36ab9530869108/src/flask/sansio/scaffold.py/#L408-L437)</code>\n> <code>[src/flask/sansio/app.py[633-649]](https://github.com/seonho12-54/qodo-coderabbit-benchmark/blob/56a0ec00080153af0afed3b70b36ab9530869108/src/flask/sansio/app.py/#L633-L649)</code>\n> <code>[src/flask/app.py[981-990]](https://github.com/seonho12-54/qodo-coderabbit-benchmark/blob/56a0ec00080153af0afed3b70b36ab9530869108/src/flask/app.py/#L981-L990)</code>\n> <code>[src/flask/views.py[124-135]](https://github.com/seonho12-54/qodo-coderabbit-benchmark/blob/56a0ec00080153af0afed3b70b36ab9530869108/src/flask/views.py/#L124-L135)</code>\n></details>\n\n> <details>\n><summary>Agent prompt</summary>\n><br/>\n>\n>```\n>The issue below was found during a code review. Follow the provided context and guidance below and implement a solution\n>\n>## Issue description\n>Explicitly setting `provide_automatic_options=True` no longer adds `OPTIONS` to the URL rule. The request consequently fails routing with 405 before automatic OPTIONS dispatch can occur.\n>\n>## Issue Context\n>Configuration should determine the value only when no explicit value or view attribute is provided. After resolving that value, `OPTIONS` must be added whenever the final value is true. Add regression coverage for both an explicit argument and a view function or class-based view attribute set to true.\n>\n>## Fix Focus Areas\n>- src/flask/sansio/app.py[633-649]\n>- tests/test_basic.py[75-127]\n>- tests/test_views.py[101-117]\n>```\n> <code>ⓘ Copy this prompt and use it to remediate the issue with your preferred AI generation tools</code>\n></details>\n\n<hr/>\n</details>\n\n\n\n<img src=\"https://www.qodo.ai/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/light-grey-line.svg\" height=\"10%\" alt=\"